sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch08-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The sterility of hybrids closely resembles the sterility induced in pure species by unnatural conditions of life: in both cases the reproductive system is disturbed independently of general health, by disturbed conditions in one case and by two organisations compounded into one in the other.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hybrid sterility resembles sterility caused by unnatural conditions";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter VIII, “Hybridism”; section “Causes of the sterility of first crosses and of hybrids”. Scope: hybrids and pure species under captivity or cultivation"
}
